  "chapter": 765,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 126 Chapter 765\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 1311-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to requir-\n        ing the Long Island Power Authority  to  prepare  a  semi-annual\n        expenditure and lobbying report\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  will  amend the Long Island Power Authority Act to require\nthe Long Island Power Authority  (LIPA)  and  its  service  provider  to\nreport  to  the  Governor and specified legislative leaders on or before\nMarch 31, 2022, and every  semi-annual  period  thereafter,  on  certain\nadvertising  and  lobbying  activities they or specified representatives\nhave engaged in during the reporting period.\n \n  The scope of this bill, particularly the object of  the  lobbying  and\nadvertising on which LIPA and its service provider would have to report,\nlack  precision and clarity. For example, the bill can be read as apply-\ning to activities unrelated to LIPA, or  in  the  case  of  the  service\nprovider, its provision of services to LIPA.\n \n  I also note that LIPA, a state public authority, is already subject to\na  level  of  transparency  that  far exceeds that of any investor-owned\nutility in the state. For example, LIPA is already  required  to  report\ndetailed  information regarding its financials and results of operations\nto the New York State Authorities Budget Office and the  Office  of  the\nState  Comptroller  (OSC).  LIPA  contracts  are  subject  to review and\napproval by the New York State Attorney General and  the  OSC.  LIPA  is\nsubject  to  the  Freedom  of  Information  Law. LIPA board meetings are\nsubject to the Open Meetings Law which requires advanced notice  of  all\nmeetings,  including  opportunities  for  the public to participate, and\nLIPA also livestreams its board and committee meetings on the  internet.\nLIPA  is also subject to Project Sunlight, which requires reporting in a\npublic database of appearances by persons seeking  to  influence  agency\ndecision-making  in areas such as ratemaking, procurement and regulatory\nmatters.\n \n  I have reached an agreement with the Legislature on  an  amendment  to\nthis  bill  that addresses the drafting issues noted above. In addition,\nthis bill will provide LIPA an opportunity to provide additional  trans-\nparency,  particularly at the local level, around its efforts to protect\nand advance the interests of its ratepayers.\n \n  Based on my agreement with the Legislature, and for the other  reasons\nstated, I am signing this bill.\n \n  The bill is approved.                          (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
